Lib4337_Test
├── when calling parseValidationData
│   ├── given validUntil is zero in the packed data
│   │   └── it should return max uint48 for validUntil
│   ├── given validUntil is non-zero in the packed data
│   │   └── it should return the exact validUntil value
│   ├── given validAfter is zero in the packed data
│   │   └── it should return zero for validAfter
│   └── given result is a non-zero address
│       └── it should return the exact address
├── when calling checkValidation
│   ├── given validAfter is greater than current timestamp
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given validUntil is less than current timestamp
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given result address is not zero
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given time bounds are valid and result is zero
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── given validation data is zero
│   │   └── it should return true
│   └── given validAfter equals current timestamp
│       └── it should return false
├── when calling intersectValidationData
│   ├── given preValidationData is zero
│   │   └── it should return validationRes via short circuit
│   ├── given validationRes is zero
│   │   └── it should return preValidationData via short circuit
│   ├── given both values are non-zero
│   │   ├── given validUntil1 is zero
│   │   │   └── it should treat validUntil1 as max uint48
│   │   ├── given validUntil2 is zero
│   │   │   └── it should treat validUntil2 as max uint48
│   │   ├── given validUntil1 is greater than validUntil2
│   │   │   └── it should use validUntil2 in the result
│   │   ├── given validUntil1 is less than or equal to validUntil2
│   │   │   └── it should use validUntil1 in the result
│   │   ├── given validAfter1 is less than validAfter2
│   │   │   └── it should use validAfter2 in the result
│   │   ├── given validAfter1 is greater than or equal to validAfter2
│   │   │   └── it should use validAfter1 in the result
│   │   ├── given either result is 1
│   │   │   └── it should return 1 as the result address
│   │   ├── given both results are 0
│   │   │   └── it should return 0 as the result address
│   │   ├── given preValidationData has aggregator and validationRes is success
│   │   │   └── it should preserve preValidationData aggregator
│   │   ├── given preValidationData is success and validationRes has aggregator
│   │   │   └── it should adopt validationRes aggregator
│   │   ├── given both have the same aggregator
│   │   │   └── it should return that aggregator
│   │   ├── given both have different aggregators
│   │   │   └── it should return 1 as the result address
│   │   ├── given preValidationData uses block number format and validationRes uses timestamp format
│   │   │   └── it should revert with ValidityFormatMismatch
│   │   ├── given preValidationData uses timestamp format and validationRes uses block number format
│   │   │   └── it should revert with ValidityFormatMismatch
│   │   └── given both use block number format
│   │       └── it should not revert and intersect correctly
│   └── given both values are zero
│       └── it should return zero
└── when calling usesBlockNumberFormat
    ├── given both validAfter and validUntil have MODE_BIT set
    │   └── it should return true
    ├── given only validAfter has MODE_BIT set
    │   └── it should return false
    ├── given only validUntil has MODE_BIT set
    │   └── it should return false
    └── given neither has MODE_BIT set
        └── it should return false
